#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054275 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f986c29-111e-5cb3-8104-62ab734f1c47" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements of an Indexed Family"}] :question/id #uuid "154d4cf7-a72a-51b1-bbb3-9bcf83b88e98" :question/math-academy-id "e-12665" :question/problem "Find $T_2$ given that $T_n = \\{1, 2, \\ldots, 2n+1 \\}$, where $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$." :question/worked-solution "To write down the elements of $T_2$, we substitute $n=2$ into the expression and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT_{2} &= {1, 2, …, 2(2) + 1} \\\\\n&= {1, 2, …, 5} \\\\\n&= {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054282 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "957a2f61-61b1-5675-ba84-5348a47af986" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unions and Intersections of Finite Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/id #uuid "60e24dac-c47a-53ee-9c91-0e6987e966f0" :question/math-academy-id "e-12763" :question/problem "Find $\\,\\displaystyle \\bigcup_{i \\in I} S_i$, given that $I = \\{-1, 0, 1 \\}$, and $S_i = (i-1, \\,i+1)$." :question/worked-solution "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n\\bigcup_{i \\in I} A_i = \\big\\{x\\in U \\:: \\: x \\in A_i \\:\\:\\textrm{for at least one} A_i,\\:\\: i \\in I \\big\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n⋃_(i ∈ I)S_{i} &= S_{-1}∪S_{0}∪S_{1} \\\\\n&= (-2, 0)∪(-1, 1)∪(0, 2) \\\\\n&= (-2, 2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054283 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c1e93acb-6c0b-5263-9df9-9dcc00680845" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unions and Intersections of (Countably) Infinite Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/id #uuid "842ee2c1-8e78-56dd-b109-b9fcc273704e" :question/math-academy-id "e-12764" :question/problem "Find $\\,\\displaystyle \\bigcap_{i \\in I} X_i$ given that $I = \\mathbb{N}$ and $X_i = \\{i, \\, 2i \\}$." :question/worked-solution "The intersection of a family of indexed sets $\\{A_i\\}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n\\bigcap_{i \\in I} A_i = \\big\\{x\\in U \\:: \\: x \\in A_i \\:\\:\\textrm{for all} A_i,\\:\\: i \\in I \\big\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=1$, we have $X_1 = \\{1, 2 \\}$\n- if $i=2$, we have $X_2 = \\{2, 4 \\}$\n- if $i=3$, we have $X_3 = \\{3, 6 \\}$\n- if $i=4$, we have $X_4 = \\{4, 8 \\}$\n\nand so on.\n\nNotice that there is no element that belongs to all the sets. Therefore,\n\n$$\n⋂_(i ∈ I)X_{i} = ∅\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054960 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f986c29-111e-5cb3-8104-62ab734f1c47" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements of an Indexed Family"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "891c57e7-7a8a-5a83-af70-6e0a6138792b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1, 2, …, 41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051702} {:answer/id #uuid "dd10fbcf-f5f8-5985-bdde-e51481dc5833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{-5,-4, …, 4, 5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051703} {:answer/id #uuid "1a08f111-d2ce-56fa-a5aa-7848cd20fe16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1, 2, 3, 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051704} {:answer/id #uuid "66e3711c-df15-5144-a652-2053423cbc5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051705} {:answer/id #uuid "6daee3a7-a690-5985-8150-de2b8d250f3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66e3711c-df15-5144-a652-2053423cbc5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051705} :answer-field/id #uuid "5034b73e-83b1-57b